# NVSK00RUS_R_20251000000_01D_30S_MO.crx.gz

Dataset: sat-doppler — Carrier-phase Doppler of 79 GPS, Galileo and GLONASS satellites at 34 IGS
  stations on 2025-04-10: orbits, station positions, GM and Ω fitted to the Doppler alone
File: data/sat/raw/NVSK00RUS_R_20251000000_01D_30S_MO.crx.gz
SHA-256: d85a8835dbb4f69197f14b5dedcbacb6df3cef978668300df34751930f7f1700 (also in
  data/sat/inputs.lock; check with: cd data/sat && sha256sum -c inputs.lock)
In the public repository: no, only this description and the hash: the file may be shared but is kept
  out of git for its size. Get it from fog fetch sat-doppler, then compare its SHA-256 with the one
  above.
Obtained: downloaded as published (fog fetch or by hand).
From: IGS daily RINEX 3 observation files, 2025 day 100, BKG open archive (the same files as
  gps-raw).
Check it yourself: fog verify sat-doppler (tools/) downloads it again into a temporary directory and
  compares it with this hash.
Collected: 2026-10-02
Licence: other — IGS data, BKG open archive (https://igs.bkg.bund.de): free, cite the IGS
  (Johnston et al. 2017). RNXCMP (crx2rnx): GSI terms, cite Hatanaka (2008).
Sources:
- IGS / BKG GNSS data centre, daily RINEX 3 observation files (30 s) and broadcast ephemeris
  BRDC00IGS, 2025 day 100 <https://igs.bkg.bund.de/root_ftp/IGS/>
- Johnston, G., Riddell, A., Hausler, G. (2017), The International GNSS Service, in Springer
  Handbook of Global Navigation Satellite Systems, 967-982
- Hatanaka, Y. (2008), A Compression Format and Tools for GNSS Observation Data, Bulletin of the
  Geospatial Information Authority of Japan, 55, 21-30 (RNXCMP)
  <https://terras.gsi.go.jp/ja/crx2rnx.html>
- Montenbruck, O., Gill, E. (2000), Satellite Orbits: Models, Methods and Applications, Springer,
  §3.2-3.3 (J2 and third-body accelerations, low-precision Sun and Moon)
Evidence class (rule 10): measure
What would vindicate the flat model (rule 5): The stations held on one plane (tilt, height and
  positions free, everything else as free as on the globe) fitting the Doppler as well as the free
  solution; or the satellites needing different GM for their periods (Kepler's third law failing).
Built by: fog build sat-doppler
Generated files:
- src/data/presets/sat-doppler.js
Code:
- tools/internal/build/satdop
